target
coverage

# Crash inputs. Deliberately NOT committed: an artifact here is a live bug, and
# the fix belongs with a deterministic regression test on stable — see the
# overflow case in `crates/verus-tx/tests/decoder_robustness.rs`. A crash file
# left lying in the repo is a bug nobody is looking at.
artifacts

# `corpus/` IS committed. It is ~280 KB of content across ~1,400 files, which
# is smaller than `fixtures/`, and it is what the CI replay step runs against:
# a seed that used to pass and now crashes is the cheapest regression signal
# there is. Run `cargo +nightly fuzz cmin <target>` before committing a grown
# corpus so it stays a coverage-preserving minimum rather than everything the
# fuzzer happened to keep.
